67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption">Photo by RFB</figcaption></figure></div><p>In the recent Budget 2026, Ireland announced it will make its Basic Income for the Arts (BIA) pilot scheme permanent starting next year. The program provides a weekly stipend of &#8364;325 to eligible artists.</p><p>An independent review of the pilot found that for every &#8364;1 of public money invested, the arts returned &#8364;1.39 to society through economic and social benefits. Artists also reported improved mental well-being and reduced financial stress.</p><p>In the U.S., the Living Wage for Musicians Act has been floated which would reform the economics of music streaming to ensure artists and musicians can earn a sustainable living from their work. But will it ever pass? Read more below...</p><p>References / Read More:</p><p><a href="https://mixmag.net/amp/irish-government-implement-basic-income-artists-scheme-2026">https://mixmag.net/amp/irish-government-implement-basic-income-artists-scheme-2026</a></p><p><a href="https://www.digitalmusicnews.com/2025/09/02/living-wage-musicians-act-congress/">https://www.digitalmusicnews.com/2025/09/02/living-wage-musicians-act-congress/</a></p> ]]>
